course: dictionary
lesson: 8686
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «Segment» is a good example. As a noun it means one of the parts something is divided into, like a segment of an orange. As a verb it means to divide something into parts.
explain: «A worm's body is made of many rings called segments, and tiny bristles on them grip the soil.» The clues are worm, body and rings, so segments must be the parts of the body. Here it is a noun, said SEG-ment.
explain: «Spelling is segmenting: you hear frog, tap one finger for each sound.» Segmenting is a verb, said seg-MENT. It means to split something into its parts, here the sounds of a word. Check it by putting your meaning in the sentence: split the word into its sounds, and it still makes sense.
fact: A segment is one of the parts that something is divided into.
fact: As a noun, segment is said SEG-ment; as a verb, it is said seg-MENT.
fact: In maths, a line segment is the part of a line between two end points.
fact: In phonics, to segment a word means to split it into its sounds: c-a-t.
fact: «Millipedes» have two pairs of legs on most body segments; «centipedes» have one pair of legs on each body segment.
exercise: «A worm's body is made of many rings called segments.» In this sentence, what is a segment? | *One of the parts a body is divided into | A tiny bristle that grips the soil | A line with no end | A kind of fast hunter
exercise: What is a line segment in maths? | A line with no ends at all | A sound in a word | *The part of a line between two end points | A circle with a straight cut
exercise: «Spelling is segmenting: you hear frog, tap one finger for each sound.» What does segmenting mean here? | To stop reading | *To split a word into its sounds | To sing a song | To spell a word backwards
test: «Scientists count the segments on each beetle foot to sort beetles into families.» Why do scientists count the segments? | *To sort beetles into families | To give beetles names | To find the sea | To make beetles run faster
test: Which sentence uses segment as a verb? | *Teachers ask pupils to segment words into sounds to help them spell | Centipedes have one pair of legs on each body segment | A segment of an orange is sweet | A short segment of the line was missing
exam: Ella says a segment of an orange should be said seg-MENT. Is she right? | Yes, every form of segment is said seg-MENT | *No, as a noun it is said SEG-ment | No, you cannot say segment at all | Yes, because segment is always a verb
